From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pdh: real counters, counter arrays, statistics, the H functions

\Processor(...)\% Processor Time was a constant raw value (FIXME 500000). The counters are now sampled: Processor (_Total and one instance per processor) % Processor Time, % User Time, % Privileged Time, % Idle Time from NtQuerySystemInformation(SystemProcessorPerformanceInformation) as 100ns timers over two samples (PDH_INVALID_DATA until the second); System Up Time, Processes, Threads; Memory Available Bytes/MBytes, Committed Bytes, Commit Limit, % Committed Bytes In Use. A counter added with the instance "*" holds every instance of its family. PdhGetFormattedCounterArrayA/W, PdhGetRawCounterArrayA/W, PdhComputeCounterStatistics, PdhFormatFromRawValue, PdhOpenQueryH and the H variants of PdhEnumObjects, PdhEnumObjectItems, PdhExpandWildCardPath, PdhGetDefaultPerfObject and PdhGetDefaultPerfCounter were spec stubs. PdhCalculateCounterFromRawValue takes raw1 as the newer sample as documented. The scale factor applies when set with PdhSetCounterScaleFactor (and PDH_FMT_NOSCALE is not given); percentages are capped at 100 unless PDH_FMT_NOCAP100.
